WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.870 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  women's rights activists shed tears of  joy for years they've been fighting for  the right to legal abortion now  colombia's constitutional court has made  it possible  this is a big achievement for all women  we want a greater recognition of our  full citizenship more security over our  bodies and over our sexual and  reproductive rights  every year colombian prosecutors open  400 cases against women accused of  having illegal abortions or those who  allegedly help them  more than 340 women have been convicted  since 2006.  until now colombian women were only  allowed to terminate pregnancies in  cases of rape fetal deformity or if the  mother's life was in danger  but even those exceptions weren't always  respected  just in 2020 4 000 girls between 10 and  14 years gave birth pregnancies in  children that young can only be the  result of rape the only explanation for  such high numbers is that women needed  more protection that's what we fought  for  four out of five judges voted in favor  of extending abortion rights despite  opposition from the catholic church and  pro-life activists who prayed in front  of the court  the feminists believe this is a step  forward for women when in reality it's a  step backwards because the fight for  women's rights doesn't include murdering  others  president ivan was opposed as well  saying the decision is too big to be  made by five judges  by allowing abortions until 24 weeks  colombia's court has raised the bar even  compared to countries which have taken  giant steps to defend women's  reproductive rights  in most countries the time limit for  having an abortion is far shorter  in the meantime women activists say it's  not enough to have their rights on paper  they say they'll keep fighting to make  sure the law is implemented monika  yanakiv al-jazeera

